{"name":"Nemesia","hex":"#ff00a0","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Nemesia","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic genus within the family Scrophulariaceae – certain plants, some called lionfaces.","A taxonomic genus within the family Nemesiidae – certain spiders."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Nemesia"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nemesia (plant)","blocks":[{"text":"Nemesia is a genus of annuals, perennials and sub-shrubs which are native to sandy coasts or disturbed ground in South Africa. Numerous hybrids have been selected, and the annual cultivars are popular with gardeners as bedding plants. In temperate regions they are usually treated as half-hardy, grown from seed in heat, and planted out after all danger of frost has passed."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Nemesia_Sunsatia_Banana.jpg/330px-Nemesia_Sunsatia_Banana.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nemesia_(plant)","wikidata":"Q2503868"},{"title":"Nemesia (spider)","blocks":[{"text":"Nemesia is a genus of mygalomorph spiders in the family Nemesiidae, first described by Jean Victoire Audouin in 1826."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Nemesia_simoni_macho.jpg/330px-Nemesia_simoni_macho.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nemesia_(spider)","wikidata":"Q2317783"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Nemesia_%27Fleurie_Blue%27_01.JPG/500px-Nemesia_%27Fleurie_Blue%27_01.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Nemesia_%27Fleurie_Blue%27_01.JPG/1280px-Nemesia_%27Fleurie_Blue%27_01.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/